  "why": "A small sewage works beside a park creek, built in the ground in section: the town's sewer pipe runs under the cut to the creek, then a settling tank and an aeration tank go into the cut, clean water returns to the creek, and the sludge goes to a digester whose gas burns as a flare. The camera opens close on the pipe pouring into the creek, follows the tanks in mid shots, and ends wide on the fenced plant.",
